  "live_records": {
    "q-186013": {
      "dom_id": "step-q186013",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$16%$ of $75$ is equal to{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $75,$ and the percentage is $16%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n16%=16÷100=0.16\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =16%\\times 75 \\\\  & =0.16\\times 75 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $16%$ of $75$ is $12.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n16%=\\frac{16}{100}=\\frac{16÷4}{100÷4}=\\frac{4}{25}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =16%\\times 75 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{25}\\times 75 \\\\  & =4\\times \\frac{75}{25} \\\\  & =4\\times 3 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $16%$ of $75$ is $12.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
