    "q-186001": {
      "dom_id": "step-q186001",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$45%$ of $120$ is equal to{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $120,$ and the percentage is $45%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n45%=45÷100=0.45\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =45%\\times 120 \\\\  & =0.45\\times 120 \\\\  & =54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $45%$ of $120$ is $54.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n45%=\\frac{45}{100}=\\frac{45÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{9}{20}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =45%\\times 120 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{20}\\times 120 \\\\  & =9\\times \\frac{120}{20} \\\\  & =9\\times 6 \\\\  & =54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $45%$ of $120$ is $54.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
