    "q-186017": {
      "dom_id": "step-q186017",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$7%$ of $500$ is equal to{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $500,$ and the percentage is $7%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n7%=7÷100=0.07\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =7%\\times 500 \\\\  & =0.07\\times 500 \\\\  & =35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7%$ of $500$ is $35.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n7%=\\frac{7}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =7%\\times 500 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{100}\\times 500 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{500}{100} \\\\  & =7\\times 5 \\\\  & =35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7%$ of $500$ is $35.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
