    "q-186008": {
      "dom_id": "step-q186008",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$70%$ of $80$ is equal to{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $80,$ and the percentage is $70%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n70%=70÷100=0.7\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =70%\\times 80 \\\\  & =0.7\\times 80 \\\\  & =56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $70%$ of $80$ is $56.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n70%=\\frac{70}{100}=\\frac{70÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{7}{10}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =70%\\times 80 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}\\times 80 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{80}{10} \\\\  & =7\\times 8 \\\\  & =56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $70%$ of $80$ is $56.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
