    "q-160842": {
      "dom_id": "step-q160842",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "What is $115%$ of $80?$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $80,$ and the percentage is $115%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n115%=115÷100=1.15\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =115%\\times 80 \\\\  & =1.15\\times 80 \\\\  & =92\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $115%$ of $80$ is $92.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n115%=\\frac{115}{100}=\\frac{115÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{23}{20}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =115%\\times 80 \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{20}\\times 80 \\\\  & =23\\times \\frac{80}{20} \\\\  & =23\\times 4 \\\\  & =92\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $115%$ of $80$ is $92.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
