    "q-61533": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61533",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "What is $120%$ of $25?$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $25,$ and the percentage is $120%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n120%=120÷100=1.2\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =120%\\times 25 \\\\  & =1.2\\times 25 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $120%$ of $25$ is $30.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n120%=\\frac{120}{100}=\\frac{120÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =120%\\times 25 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\times 25 \\\\  & =6\\times \\frac{25}{5} \\\\  & =6\\times 5 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $120%$ of $25$ is $30.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
