    "q-160859": {
      "dom_id": "step-q160859",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "What is $0.25%$ of $400?$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $400,$ and the percentage is $0.25%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.25%=0.25÷100=0.0025\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.25%\\times 400 \\\\  & =0.0025\\times 400 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.25%$ of $400$ is $1.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.25%=\\frac{0.25}{100}=\\frac{0.25\\times 100}{100\\times 100}=\\frac{25}{10,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.25%\\times 400 \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{10,000}\\times 400 \\\\  & =\\frac{10,000}{10,000} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.25%$ of $400$ is $1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
